WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.413 --> 00:00:17.564
"The boys from the next town are playing Paper Chase today," said Bobbie one morning.

2
00:00:17.584 --> 00:00:20.847
"Perks thinks they'll run along the railway line.

3
00:00:21.187 --> 00:00:22.128
We can go and watch."

4
00:00:23.128 --> 00:00:25.490
Mother gave the children some lunch, and they left.

5
00:00:27.752 --> 00:00:32.076
There were men working on the tracks, using different tools like spades and shovels.

6
00:00:33.152 --> 00:00:34.674
The children watched them for a while.

7
00:00:36.155 --> 00:00:38.717
Then a voice said, "Let me pass, please."

8
00:00:39.858 --> 00:00:41.360
It was the first boy from the school.

9
00:00:41.380 --> 00:00:43.081
"He's 'it.'"

10
00:00:43.982 --> 00:00:46.004
Bobbie explained the game to her brother and sister.

11
00:00:46.024 --> 00:00:49.267
"All the other boys have to chase after him."

12
00:00:50.368 --> 00:00:53.331
Under the boy's arm was a bag full of little pieces of paper.

13
00:00:54.993 --> 00:00:58.256
The boy dropped a piece of paper behind him for the other boys to follow.

14
00:00:59.296 --> 00:01:03.860
The children watched as he ran into the long dark tunnel, dropping more paper behind him.

15
00:01:05.201 --> 00:01:06.482
The workmen watched him too.

16
00:01:06.502 --> 00:01:09.264
"He shouldn't go in there," said one.

17
00:01:09.284 --> 00:01:12.927
"It's only a game," said another.

18
00:01:14.028 --> 00:01:18.031
Then the other boys came, running and following the little white pieces of paper.

19
00:01:19.372 --> 00:01:22.635
Bobbie and Phyllis and Peter counted the boys as they ran past.

20
00:01:23.595 --> 00:01:24.536
There were thirty of them.

21
00:01:25.877 --> 00:01:28.840
The boys ran into the tunnel and disappeared into the deep darkness.

22
00:01:30.036 --> 00:01:31.637
The last boy wore a red shirt.

23
00:01:31.657 --> 00:01:35.820
"It's not easy running in the dark," said one of the workmen.

24
00:01:36.901 --> 00:01:38.062
"How long will it take?"

25
00:01:38.442 --> 00:01:40.463
Peter asked, eyeing the long tunnel.

26
00:01:41.344 --> 00:01:42.224
It went through a hill.

27
00:01:42.245 --> 00:01:45.347
"An hour or more," the man said.

28
00:01:45.367 --> 00:01:50.970
"Let's go across the top of the hill," said Peter.

29
00:01:50.991 --> 00:01:54.053
"We can watch the boys come out the other end."

30
00:01:55.113 --> 00:01:58.576
The children climbed up the steep hill, over rocks and tree trunks.

31
00:01:59.680 --> 00:02:01.320
"It's like climbing the Alps!"

32
00:02:01.781 --> 00:02:03.161
said Bobbie, out of breath.

33
00:02:04.701 --> 00:02:05.862
At last they reached the top.

34
00:02:07.242 --> 00:02:10.023
Peter lay down on the grass, and the girls lay down too.

35
00:02:12.503 --> 00:02:13.984
After a while Bobbie sat up.

36
00:02:15.104 --> 00:02:16.324
"Look!" she cried.

37
00:02:16.345 --> 00:02:18.645
"What?" said Phyllis.

38
00:02:18.665 --> 00:02:21.546
"The view," said Bobbie.

39
00:02:21.566 --> 00:02:25.987
"Let's go now," said Peter.

40
00:02:26.007 --> 00:02:29.088
"But this view is fantastic!"

41
00:02:29.468 --> 00:02:30.329
insisted Bobbie.

42
00:02:31.350 --> 00:02:35.814
They could see the fields, the village, the station and even their white house.

43
00:02:35.834 --> 00:02:38.836
"We'll miss the paper chase!"

44
00:02:39.277 --> 00:02:40.518
said Phyllis impatiently.

45
00:02:40.538 --> 00:02:41.639
"Come on.

46
00:02:41.679 --> 00:02:42.239
Let's go."

47
00:02:43.520 --> 00:02:46.363
They climbed down until they were level with the top of the tunnel.

48
00:02:47.203 --> 00:02:47.664
They waited.

49
00:02:47.684 --> 00:02:53.609
"The boys have all gone past already, of course," said Phyllis, annoyed.

50
00:02:53.629 --> 00:02:58.372
"I don't think so," said Bobbie.

51
00:02:58.392 --> 00:03:01.633
"But even if they have, there's a wonderful view here too!

52
00:03:02.694 --> 00:03:04.715
We can see the trains come out of the tunnel.

53
00:03:05.755 --> 00:03:08.036
We've never seen the trains from on top before."

54
00:03:11.918 --> 00:03:12.718
here he comes!"

55
00:03:13.138 --> 00:03:14.279
Peter shouted at last.

56
00:03:15.839 --> 00:03:18.460
The first boy with the paper came slowly out of the tunnel.

57
00:03:20.021 --> 00:03:21.422
Soon after came the other boys.

58
00:03:22.682 --> 00:03:23.823
Some looked very tired.

59
00:03:23.843 --> 00:03:25.943
"What will we do now?"

60
00:03:26.364 --> 00:03:28.300
asked Bobbie.

61
00:03:28.320 --> 00:03:30.541
"That's not the last one," Peter said.

62
00:03:30.561 --> 00:03:33.161
"Where's the boy in the red shirt?"

63
00:03:34.382 --> 00:03:37.223
They waited a long time, but the boy did not appear.

64
00:03:38.063 --> 00:03:41.624
The children began to worry, and they climbed down to the train tracks.

65
00:03:42.744 --> 00:03:45.585
"Perhaps he had an accident," said Phyllis.

66
00:03:45.605 --> 00:03:49.206
"Let's go and look," said Bobbie.

67
00:03:50.466 --> 00:03:53.207
They slowly walked a few steps into the dark tunnel.

68
00:03:53.947 --> 00:03:55.868
But they couldn't see a boy in a red shirt.

69
00:03:57.021 --> 00:03:59.789
It was very dark and water dripped down the wall.

70
00:03:59.809 --> 00:04:02.617
"I don't like it in here!"

71
00:04:03.058 --> 00:04:04.763
said Phyllis, looking frightened.
